		"about": "The verbs lessons are made for, most used first, each with the English the learner reads: base, she-form, before, and the ing form. Part 1 of every job is the grid's own lesson, so the first verb here is Part 2. All of them stand on their own, without an object, so 我吃了 is a sentence and 我使了 would not be. `stative` verbs sound wrong in English as 'I am knowing' or 'Know!' and sit out those two jobs; `no-going` and `no-command` leave out one job each. The before of know is 'found out': 我知道了 is the moment of learning it. `no-going` marks the verbs that do not take 在 on their own (我在来, 我在坐): going and coming, sitting and standing, beginning and ending. Left out on purpose: 去, which the grid's own lessons teach; 是 and 有, which need lessons of their own; 要, 能 and 会, which are the want-can-must job; 读, whose English is the same now and before; and 睡觉, whose 了 says going to bed, not having slept.",
